sequenceDiagram
    participant Client as Inference Client
    participant Ingress as Platform Ingress / Gateway<br/>443/TCP HTTPS (platform-dependent)
    participant Svc as isvc-predictor Service<br/>80/TCP → 8080
    participant Init as storage-initializer<br/>(init container)
    participant Store as Object Storage<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant Vol as /mnt/models volume
    participant Server as autogluonserver<br/>8080/TCP HTTP (plaintext)
    participant AG as AutoGluon Predictor<br/>(in-process)

    Note over Init,AG: Flow 1: Model load at startup
    Init->>Store: GET model artifacts<br/>HTTPS/443 TLS, storage credentials
    Store-->>Init: Model directory
    Init->>Vol: Write model files
    Server->>Vol: Storage.download (local passthrough)
    Server->>AG: version_compat check, then TimeSeriesPredictor.load
    alt Not a time-series model
        Server->>AG: TabularPredictor.load (unpickle)
    end
    AG-->>Server: Predictor loaded (ready)

    Note over Client,AG: Flow 2: Tabular inference
    Client->>Ingress: POST predict<br/>Bearer token (if platform auth enabled)
    Ingress->>Svc: Forward
    Svc->>Server: POST /v1/models/{m}:predict or /v2/models/{m}/infer<br/>HTTP/8080, no auth at container
    Server->>AG: predict() or predict_proba() (PREDICT_PROBA)
    AG-->>Server: Labels / class probabilities
    Server-->>Client: JSON response (v1 predictions / v2 outputs)

    Note over Client,AG: Flow 3: Time-series forecast (REST v1 only)
    Client->>Server: POST /v1/models/{m}:predict<br/>JSON instances + optional known_covariates<br/>HTTP/8080 (TLS upstream at platform)
    Server->>AG: TimeSeriesPredictor.predict()
    AG-->>Server: Forecast (mean + quantiles)
    Server-->>Client: predictions with id / timestamp / mean / quantiles
